  "findings": [
    "PSS definitions vs built-in PSA; validating-admission scope, workload-template warn/audit vs resulting Pod enforcement, non-eviction of existing Pods and best-effort enforce-label preview corrected.",
    "Baseline explicit NET_RAW/hostPath/hostPort controls, valid runAsUser field, Restricted readOnlyRootFilesystem recommendation, policy-v1.35 user-namespace relaxations and Restricted procMount boundary verified with upstream library.",
    "Unsafe all-namespace overwrite replaced by explicit one-namespace observation update, existing-label refusal and resourceVersion condition; existing-Pod preview uses enforce rather than warn.",
    "False-green CI grep replaced by explicit Pod-only server-dry-run procedure with positive/negative controls and failure propagation for credentials, empty inputs, wrong namespace/kind, missing enforcement and unexpected negative-control outcomes.",
    "Exact request-username/runtimeClass/namespace exemption semantics; EKS managed control-plane boundary; privileged namespace profile is not a static exemption; RuntimeClass alone neither installs runtime nor exempts; Kyverno cannot override PSA denial.",
    "Root nginx/readOnly/port mismatch corrected using upstream OCI digest metadata (amd64/arm64, user101, Nginx1.30.4), writable /tmp and matching 8080 ConfigMap/probes; no image execution claimed.",
    "Invented pod-security-webhook metric and namespace label removed; actual pod_security_evaluations_total with evaluation vs API-rejection and missing-series limits.",
    "PSP commands/objects retained as historical <=1.24 only; mapping is not equivalence; no automatic downgrade of existing enforcement; migration day ranges explicitly illustrative.",
    "All original headings/topics and 12questions per locale retained; 160 original rendered IDs preserved with two explicit quiz aliases; 4currentMD actualVitePress/Vue compiles passed.",
    "All six figure specs fully read; factual captions added; six parent-owned figure repairs remain and keep the two guides needs_followup."
